---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_637",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 637,
  "text": "[[2775.5]] <b>494₁.  Erster Ansatz ERSTER ANSATZ </p>\n<p> [[2775.8]] Propositum nobis est in Legum juris civilis rationes inquirere, ut eas interpretari\n[[2775.9]] possimus. Jurisconsulti enim est non verba tantum legum tenere, sed <i>vim et potestatem</i> l.\n[[2775.10]] 17. D. <i>de Legibus</i>. </p>\n<p> [[2775.11]] Est autem <b>Lex</b>, enuntiatio dirigens actiones humanas vim cogendi habens. Omnis\n[[2775.12]] enuntiatio capax est interpretationis, et duplex est interpretatio, una dicti <greek>toỹ ȓhtoỹ</greek>,\n[[2775.13]] altera sententiae <greek>th̃w dianoíaw</greek>: interdum enim verba obscura sunt, sive ob homonymiam\n[[2775.14]] aut tropos singulorum verborum, sive ob amphiboliam aut figuras quae in connexione\n[[2775.15]] verborum deprehenduntur. De Homonymiis vid. Arist[otelis] lib. 1. <i>Top</i>[<i>icorum</i>] cap. 13.,\n[[2775.16]] de metaphoris aliisque tropis tum in <i>Rhetor</i>[<i>ica</i>]; tum in <i>Arte poetica</i>: interdum clare\n[[2775.17]] quidem locutus est Legislator, sed aliud dixit quam in mente habuit. Dixit autem vel\n[[2775.18]] disparatum pro disparato quod rarius est, vel dixit genus pro specie, aut speciem pro\n[[2775.19]] genere. Priore casu opus est restrictione, posteriore opus est extensione verborum.\n[[2775.20]] Sententia autem Legislatoris, seu quid in mente habuerit, cognitum erit, si rationes quae\n[[2775.21]] illum ad legem ferendam movere nobis sint compertae. Nam ex praesumta Legislatoris\n[[2776.1]] voluntate legem latam ad similia extendemus, l. <i>non possunt</i> 12. D. <i>de Legibus</i>. Ita lex\n[[2776.2]] <i>duodecim tabularum</i> proximum agnatum tutorem esse jusserat, cujus ratio esse videtur,\n[[2776.3]] quia ubi successionis commodum est, ibi tutelae onus esse debet; quin imo qui spem\n[[2776.4]] succedendi habet providere potest, ne Patrimonium depereat. Itaque et imponi tutelam\n[[2776.5]] invito successori aequum est, et non denegari volenti. Quaeritur jam quis liberti sit tutor,\n[[2776.6]] dicendum est, ipsum patronum, qui impuberem manumisit, nam et ille successionis\n[[2776.7]] commodum habet. Similiter ob praesumtam voluntatem legislatoris legem generalem ex\n[[2776.8]] aequitate restringemus, haec enim est natura aequitatis. </p>\n<p> [[2776.9]] Rationes quae legislatorem movere vel malo vel bono titulo censentur. Malum\n[[2776.10]] titulum habent, quae sumuntur ex affectibus ejus aut privata utilitate cum publico bono\n[[2776.11]] pugnante; ex hujusmodi rationibus nullum jus sumitur neque ad consequentias possunt\n[[2776.12]] trahi, professa enim injustitia non nisi per vim obtinet. Quae bonum titulum habent, sunt\n[[2776.13]] verae vel apparentes. Apparentes, quae nituntur principiis quibusdam specie justi et aequi\n[[2776.14]] a legislatore efformatis, quae licet erronea sint, aut parum accurata, tamen sequenda sunt,\n[[2776.15]] neque enim privatorum aut Magistratuum inferiorum est abrogare leges, et corrigere\n[[2776.16]] legislatorem, cum fieri possit, ut ipsimet errent, qui Legislatorem erroris accusant. Verae\n[[2776.17]] rationes sumuntur vel ex jure naturae vel ex ratione status; et spectatur vel virtus civium\n[[2776.18]] vel sufficientia rerum; et rationes quae tempore legislatoris valebant vel subsistunt adhuc,\n[[2776.19]] vel mutato rerum statu cessant, sed non ideo lex cessat, licet minus sit favorabilis.\n[[2776.20]] Hujusmodi rationes non cuivis loco seu civitati, nec cuivis civitatis tempori convenientes,\n[[2776.21]] postulant cognitionem historiae et Geographiae, ex quibus propositio minor seu assumtio\n[[2776.22]] syllogismi discenda est, quemadmodum propositio major ex Ethicis politicisque. </p>\n<p> [[2776.23]] Rationem alicujus propositionis accurate reddere, est eam a priori demonstrare.\n[[2776.24]] Principia demonstrationum sunt <b>definitiones</b> et <b>axiomata</b>. Quibus accedunt nonnunquam\n[[2776.25]] <b>experimenta</b>, et propositiones quaedam concessae sive assumtae quas\n[[2776.26]] vocant <b>hypotheses</b>; et denique <b>theoremata</b>, tam ante demonstrata. Sed nunc sufficiat\n[[2776.27]] modum exponere definitiones et axiomata investigandi et ex illis demonstrandi.\n[[2776.28]] Demonstratio est syllogismus scientiam pariens. Scire est rem per causam nosse, seu\n[[2777.1]] nosse causam cur affectio aliqua subjecto insit. Quae petenda est ex essentia subjecti sive\n[[2777.2]] definitione. Definitio Rei investigatur, si aliae res complures sumantur, quae de re\n[[2777.3]] praedicantur, vel de quibus ipsa praedicatur, sive sint ejus individua, sive species, sive\n[[2777.4]] genera, sive affectiones; et semper quaeratur ratio, cur unum de altero dicatur. In diversis\n[[2777.5]] enim diversae occurrent rationes, velut totidem genera, quae inter se juncta partes definitionis\n[[2777.6]] integrae dabunt; diversa enim genera sibi mutuo differentiarum loco sunt. Quod\n[[2777.7]] si eadem methodo generum genera quaerantur, veniemus tandem ad summa seu universalissima\n[[2777.8]] nostrae disciplinae genera, et offerent se nobis axiomata seu propositiones\n[[2777.9]] generalissimae, in quibus de generibus universalissimis etiam affectiones universalissimae\n[[2777.10]] praedicentur. Ab hisce dividendo iterum descendimus ad inferiora et demonstramus\n[[2777.11]] partim de speciebus subsumendo attributa generum, partim proprias affectiones de speciebus\n[[2777.12]] demonstrando, quae ex pluribus generum attributis inter se junctis conflantur. </p>\n",
  "number": "494₁.",
  "title": "Erster Ansatz",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:494₁. Erster Ansatz ERSTER ANSATZ Propositum nobis est in Legum juris civilis rationes inquirere, ut eas interpretari possimus. Jurisconsulti enim est non verba tantum legum tenere, sed vim et potestatem l. 17. D. de Legibus. Est autem Lex, enuntiatio dirigens actiones humanas vim cogendi habens. Om...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>